---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.13.0
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - commit
  - base
  - pr_number
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lint_command
optional_variables:
  - layer_prs
defaults:
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: each numbered deliverable is written; lint passes. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <layer-prs><![CDATA[{{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer-prs>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before any claim, run `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`; when it prints `false` follow a1. Run `test -n "{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}" && test -n "{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}"` or refuse `SANITY.PR_REQUIRED`. Then run `gh pr view {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --json baseRefName,headRefName,headRefOid --jq '.baseRefName + " " + .headRefName + " " + .headRefOid'`; require, else `SANITY.NOT_STACKED`: base `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` and head `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`; `gh api 'repos/{owner}/{repo}/stacks' --paginate --jq '.[]'` (GitHub's stacks, never local `gh stack` tracking) must have an open stack whose `pull_requests` include {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} with `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` the `head.ref` of the open PR before it (the stack's `base.ref` for its first open PR), or, in no open stack, be layer 0 awaiting layer 1: `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` is `<pr_target>` below and `gh pr list --head {{ base | string | cdata_escape }} --state open --json headRefName` prints `[]`; then `git fetch origin`, and unless `<pr_target>` = `bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.pr_target'` (a lower bound; a poured dev bead's is its `metadata.sprint_bead`'s, and none skips this check) is `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}`, `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<pr_target> origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` exits 0 (a `<pr_target>` gone from origin holds when a PR in `gh pr list --head <pr_target> --state merged --json mergeCommit` has its merge commit in `origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}`). Run `git log --format=%H origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}..{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }} | grep -q .` or refuse `SANITY.ZERO_DELTA`; run `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }} {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` or refuse `SANITY.NOT_REBASED`; run `test -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no | grep -v -e ' \.beads\.gate\.lock$' -e ' \.sc-compose/')"` or refuse `SANITY.DIRTY_TREE` (the ignored paths are `IGNORED_STATUS_PATHS` in `scripts/assignment-gates.py`); run `bd history {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` and refuse `SANITY_FROZEN` when it records a prior PASS. Only a mismatch is one of these codes: a command that fails to run (`gh`, `git fetch`, `bd`: a nonzero exit or error, not an answer) refuses `GATE_CANNOT_RUN`, a serious failure announced as in `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role. Reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Otherwise claim and start the check.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[When it prints `false` the bead is not ready: do not claim it and do not start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Report it to the task assigner: the bead, why it is not ready, and which bead or agent has to move. Then wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once, with `--layer-pr <n>` for each PR in `<layer-prs>` (empty: the single range from `<base>`), and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Preserve both raw result arrays. Record each reviewer's completion epoch when its last reply or timeout envelope arrives, before merging or waiting for shared lint; merge it as soon as it finishes with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Do not append history until selected merge determines the final verdict. Build one strict selection array with one entry per deliverable, recording the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; stdin is ignored. Append history in exact order `sanity-llm`, then `sanity-jev`, passing both rows the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Copy only the `sanity-selected` vars to `<scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` for steps e/e1. Exit 4 waits for shared lint and retries reuse supplied epochs; selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[PASS: For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the task assigner) and cite it in notes. Then close the bead and the task together: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "PASS at <sha>"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/dev-sanity-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` with `verdict` PASS. Closing the bead releases every dev bead that required `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`.]]></step>
    <step id="e1"><![CDATA[Selected FAIL only: the sanity bead must stay **open**, because closing it would release dependent dev beads. Preserve every finding unchanged. For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the task assigner) and cite it in notes. Before closing this task, run this exact command against the merge-created vars file; it creates one open `bug` child per finding under `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`, copies the report fields verbatim to child metadata and description, and adds each declared inter-finding blocking edge. Use `--reviewer sc-sanity-selected`; each child records the selected LLM/JEV source. Checker defects create no child; the selection record and workflow-issue class bead carry their evidence. Do not otherwise edit the checked parent:

```bash
{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-create-findings \
  --task {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --bead {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} \
  --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json \
  --reviewer sc-sanity-selected \
  --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY" > <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-finding-children.json
```

`sanity-create-findings` creates finding children and only their declared inter-finding prerequisite edges. It never creates a finding-sanity gate or adds an edge to another planned sprint: the phase's plan file is the sole authority for sprint-to-sprint dependencies.

The script gives each blocking child priority `clamp(parent priority - 1, P1, P4)` and copies the parent's required difficulty. The parent/child hierarchy itself is the parent closure gate; `bd` rejects a parent-to-child `blocks` edge because that would deadlock the child. For each report `depends_on` selector, the script creates `<dependent-finding-child> --blocks--> <prerequisite-finding-child>`, preventing the dependent fix from closing first. It adds the ordered `finding_bead_ids` array to the same vars file used by `atm task close`, so the final report links directly to every child; do not write those ids to parent notes because the graph is authoritative. Then reopen the checked bead with `bd reopen {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "sanity FAIL at <sha>: <n> findings" --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"`; this sanity bead's `blocks` edge re-blocks it. Return the sanity bead to the queue with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FAIL at <sha>: <n> findings"`, then close the task with the same `atm task close … completed` command and `verdict` FAIL. A failure to create or wire every child is cannot-run, not a completed FAIL. The task assigner reviews the created child beads and assigns the dev fix; the lead may overrule, amend, split, or reassign children. The parent cannot close until all children close; only then may final parent closure occur, after which the next sanity run is ready.]]></step>
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[If the selected check cannot run (plan not splittable, worktree missing, commit not pushed, a check timed out or was rejected twice), reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "<code>; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`.]]></step>
    <step id="e3"><![CDATA[After the close, render the console table as the canonical coordinator specifies (`tail -n 20` of the phase ledger through `jq -s '{runs: .}'` into `templates/sanity-run-table.md.j2`). Include the rendered table in the user-visible completion reply before reading ATM again. Report `SANITY.STATUS_TABLE_UNAVAILABLE` and the error if the ledger or render fails, without changing any verdict. Pre-dispatch refusals have no reviewer row.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the close and the required user-visible completion reply in step e3 (whenever reviewer results exist), read ATM again.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
